From 67896b31d67c9eff57d721c7a91c5ea348c05eaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:56:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 365/638] [AROS] Pass framed Mojo traffic between Processes

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model
AI_STATUS: cross-process-channel-runtime-pass
ROOT_CAUSE: AROS was still forced into Chromium single-process mode despite having independently scheduled Processes and working shared-address-space launch primitives.
FIX_REASON: Add a focused parent/child ChannelAros probe that hands an endpoint through the real command line, launches with CreateNewProc, exchanges framed messages, transfers another endpoint, and waits for child exit.
SCOPE: mojo/core/BUILD.gn; mojo/core/channel_aros_process_probe.cc
VALIDATION: Hosted 16 GiB run identified parent PID 18 and child PID 29, reported child and parent PASS framed=2 handles=1, and exited zero in 8.01 seconds.
RISK: Direct Channel traffic is proven; NodeController invitations, service binding, and browser/renderer role startup remain next.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: same-Process Channel PASS -> LaunchProcess endpoint handoff -> child endpoint recovery -> independent IO pumps -> duplex frames -> attached handle -> clean child exit.
Evidence:-channel-aros-process-20260728
Job:
---
 mojo/core/BUILD.gn                      |  15 +-
 mojo/core/channel_aros_process_probe.cc | 219 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 233 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 mojo/core/channel_aros_process_probe.cc

